This assessment followed the Penetration Testing Execution Standard (PTES) phases: pre-engagement interactions, intelligence gathering, threat modeling, vulnerability analysis, exploitation, post-exploitation, and reporting. Activity counts per phase, derived from the actual tool invocations and findings recorded during this run (not assumed), are listed in the PTES Mapping section below.

Network service assessment was performed by the Network Vulnerability Assessment Agent (external component, integrated via the documented contract in docs/network_graph_contract.md). Web application assessment used Python httpx for fingerprinting, Katana for endpoint discovery{% if crawling_enabled %} (enabled for this assessment){% else %} (not enabled for this assessment){% endif %}, and OWASP ZAP for passive security analysis{% if active_scan_enabled %} and authorised active verification{% else %} (active verification was not enabled for this assessment){% endif %}. Binary analysis used Ghidra Headless Analyzer alongside file/readelf/checksec for static identification and weakness heuristics; supplied binaries were never executed.

Every tool invocation was checked against the assessment's authorisation policy by the Scope Guard immediately before execution; denied operations are recorded in the execution log and are not reflected as findings.
